{"name":"Voyager","hex":"#4d5062","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"voyager","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who voyages, traveller, a person who explores new lands and worlds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/voyager"}],"entries":[{"title":"LG Voyager","blocks":[{"text":"The LG VX10000, also known as the Verizon Voyager or LG VX10K, is an Internet-enabled multimedia smartphone designed by LG Electronics and carried by Verizon Wireless in the US, Telus and Bell Mobility in Canada, and Reliance in Asia. The external screen is touch enabled with a virtual keyboard and buttons. It features an internal screen for use with the included full QWERTY keyboard. Both screens of the Voyager have WQVGA resolution. The Voyager's functions include those of a camera phone and a portable media player, in addition to text messaging, and Internet services including e-mail and web browsing. It is a dual-band mobile phone that uses the CDMA standard. It supports the EVDO data technology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/LG_Voyager_VX10000_External.jpg/330px-LG_Voyager_VX10000_External.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LG_Voyager"},{"title":"NCR Voyager","blocks":[{"text":"The NCR Voyager was an SMP computer platform produced by the NCR Corporation circa 1985. It used the Micro Channel bus, was based initially on the Intel 486 and predated the Intel SMP specification. Linux support for some models existed between 2005 and 2010. Later models supported up to 32 CPU using the Intel Pentium Pro."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NCR_Voyager"},{"title":"Voyager (Australian band)","blocks":[{"text":"Voyager are an Australian progressive metal band from Perth, Western Australia, formed in 1999. They have released eight studio albums. Their latest, Fearless in Love, was released in 2023. The band represented Australia in the Eurovision Song Contest 2023 with the song \"Promise\", finishing in ninth place."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Eurovision_2023_-_Jury_Semi-final_2_-_Australia_-_Voyager_%2804%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Eurovision_2023_-_Jury_Semi-final_2_-_Australia_-_Voyager_%2804%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voyager_(Australian_band)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/LG_Voyager_VX10000_Internal.jpg/500px-LG_Voyager_VX10000_Internal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/LG_Voyager_VX10000_Internal.jpg/1280px-LG_Voyager_VX10000_Internal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/LG_Voyager_VX10000_Internal.jpg/500px-LG_Voyager_VX10000_Internal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Voyager in its open state, revealing the internal screen and QWERTY keyboard.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALG_Voyager_VX10000_Internal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/LG_Voyager_VX10000_titanium.jpg/330px-LG_Voyager_VX10000_titanium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/LG_Voyager_VX10000_titanium.jpg/330px-LG_Voyager_VX10000_titanium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Titanium Voyager","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALG_Voyager_VX10000_titanium.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Voyager_%40_Euroblast_Festival_61.jpg/500px-Voyager_%40_Euroblast_Festival_61.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con